<speak>If that routine works for you, there is no need to abandon the paper diary. We can make future invitations easy to recognise, with a straightforward subject line and a brief description of the purpose. You can then place them in whichever calendar you use, without having to interpret a vague heading. For ordinary relationship meetings, some clients prefer a recurring general window while others prefer to arrange each meeting separately. We can work around either approach. The important administrative point is that you are not left wondering whether a calendar entry is a telephone conversation, a branch visit, or simply a reminder.</speak>